/-! `Ã` along the innermost axis as a word-program primitive. On word tapes:
the input words of all lines, the weight words, the parameter rulers, the
counters and the zero accumulators. The rulers and counters are unsealed to
raw strings, the word lists turned into records, the quasi-linear line loop
`LineApply.programF` runs, the output records become one paper array (most
significant bit first), and every parameter is sealed again; the input lines
and weights are consumed (`lineAPrim`). Generated by `lapgen.py`. -/

@[expose] public section


namespace IntegerMultBounds.Machine.LineAPrim

open OrderedSelect (inTape start flat)
open GaussianLine (wordRecs wordRecs_length outWords)
